  data:
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Introduction
    description: "ICT stands for \"Information and Communication Technology.\" It
      is a broad term that encompasses all technologies used to manipulate and communicate
      information. This includes computers, software, networks, telecommunications,
      the internet, and various other technologies and tools used for data storage,
      processing, and communication. The exciting world of Information and Communication
      Technology, or ICT, is like a big digital playground with lots of different
      sectors to explore. Imagine it as a giant puzzle with many pieces, and each
      piece represents a unique career or business opportunity. Whether you're passionate
      about creating cool apps, designing graphics, establishing network connectivity,
      being a call center agent, or even starting your own tech company someday,
      there's a place for you in ICT.\r\n \r\nWe have different sectors of ICT which
      are: Computer Programming, Digital Arts, Computer System Servicing and Contact
      Center Services.\r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Career and Business Opportunities of ICT
    description: "C. Computer System Servicing \u2013 Is a service that includes
      installing and configuring computer systems, establishing computer networks
      and servers, and performing maintenance and repairs on both computer systems
      and networks."
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: Career Opportunities in Computer System Servicing
    description: "Computer Assembler \u2013 A person or a technician who is responsible
      for physically assembling and building computer systems. This involves putting
      together all the hardware components of a computer, such as the central processing
      unit (CPU), motherboard, memory (RAM), storage drives, power supply, graphics
      card, and other peripherals like keyboard, mouse, and monitor.\r\nComputer
      Service Technician \u2013Also called IT Support Technician, is a professional
      who specializes in providing technical support and maintenance for computer
      systems and related equipment. Their primary responsibilities include diagnosing
      and resolving hardware and software issues, performing system upgrades, installing
      and configuring computer components, and ensuring that computer systems are
      running efficiently.\r\nNetwork Technician \u2013 Also known as a Network Support
      Technician or Network Administrator, is a professional responsible for the
      installation, configuration, maintenance, and troubleshooting of computer networks
      within an organization. Their primary role is to ensure that the network infrastructure
      operates smoothly and securely to facilitate communication and data exchange
      among various devices and users.\r\n"
    has3dView: 0
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display: []
    titleName: 'Business Opportunities in Computer System Servicing

'
    description: 'Business opportunities in Computer System Servicing can be diverse
      and lucrative, catering to the growing demand for IT services and support.
      Here are some potential avenues for entrepreneurs and businesses in this field:

      Computer
      Repair and Maintenance Services

      Start a computer repair and maintenance
      business, offering on-site or remote technical support to individuals and businesses.
      This can include diagnosing and fixing hardware and software issues, providing
      routine maintenance, and offering data recovery services.

      Managed IT
      Services

      Provide comprehensive IT management services to small and
      medium-sized businesses. This may include proactive monitoring, network management,
      security solutions, and regular system updates, all designed to keep clients''
      IT infrastructure running smoothly.

      Computer Sales and Customization

      Sell
      computers, laptops, and hardware components. Offer customization services,
      where customers can choose specific hardware configurations tailored to their
      needs.

      IT Consultancy

      Offer IT consultancy services to businesses,
      helping them optimize their IT infrastructure, plan for technology upgrades,
      and ensure data security and compliance with industry standards.

      Data
      Backup and Recovery Services

      Specialize in data backup and recovery
      solutions. Offer automated backup services, data restoration, and disaster
      recovery planning for businesses concerned about data loss.

      Cybersecurity
      Services

      With the increasing threat of cyberattacks, provide cybersecurity
      services such as vulnerability assessments, penetration testing, and the implementation
      of security measures to protect businesses from data breaches and cyber threats.

      Cloud
      Computing Solutions

      Offer cloud computing services, including cloud
      migration, management, and support. Help businesses leverage cloud technology
      to enhance scalability and reduce infrastructure costs.

      Computer Training
      and Education

      Provide computer training programs and workshops for
      individuals and organizations looking to enhance their IT skills. This can
      include courses on software applications, IT security, and hardware maintenance.

      Computer
      Networking Services

      Specialize in computer networking solutions, including
      the design, installation, and maintenance of local area networks (LANs) and
      wide area networks (WANs) for businesses.

      Remote IT Support

      Offer
      remote IT support services, providing quick solutions to computer problems
      and software issues without the need for an on-site visit.

      Computer
      Accessories and Peripherals

      Sell computer accessories, peripherals,
      and IT-related products like printers, routers, and external hard drives.

'
    has3dView: 0
